## Inspected prerequisites and exact interfaces

The current batch-8 manifest has the required compact Borel-localization page. loadStep1Record and step1Decision were run against the current frontier. These direct in-run suppliers have current hash-bound ready records:

- lem-qftx-rational-torus-classifying-space-cohomology (batch 8, level 0): T_c=(R/Z)^r, right product Milnor model, H*(BT_c;Q)=Q[u_1,...,u_r], character lattice Z^r, and c_1(L_chi)=sum_i n_i u_i; its proof states AC.
- lem-qftx-module-localization-preserves-exactness (batch 8, level 0): localization by a multiplicative set excluding zero is exact, with the zero-fraction argument.
- lem-qftx-compact-manifold-cohomology-positive-ideal-nilpotent (batch 8, level 1): for compact smooth F, H^{>0}(F;Q) is nilpotent; the proof gives finite good-cover/nerve reasoning and states AC.
- lem-qftx-borel-base-is-paracompact-of-cw-type (batch 8, level 1) is an additional direct prerequisite for the proper-fixed-normal Euler argument. Its current Step-1 record is also hash-current ready; it proves BT times F paracompact Hausdorff and of CW type for compact smooth F.

Read the current proofs and matched these hypotheses against the use. The required external mathematical suppliers were also read at their actual current files:

- def-equivariant-borel-moore-homology-and-correspondence-convolution: G=product GL_n(C), characteristic-zero coefficients, normalized omega_X^G|_X=omega_X, stable general-linear Stiefel approximations, proper pushforward, and refined diagonal operation. T=(GL_1)^r is in scope; AC is explicit.
- thm-constructible-six-functors-proper-base-change-and-verdier-duality: separated finite-type complex varieties, characteristic zero and product-general-linear actions; normalized dualizing shift, support localization, proper trace, and base-change hypotheses inspected in the full current proof. A precheck-only stamp is not being treated as mathematical approval or a gap.
- def-euler-class-by-zero-section-pullback-of-the-thom-class, lem-complex-oriented-diagonal-thom-class-realizes-the-six-functor-exchange-on-supports, thm-fixed-point-schemes-and-centralizers-of-linearly-reductive-actions, lem-multiplicative-type-groups-are-linearly-reductive, and thm-thom-isomorphism-for-oriented-vector-bundles: current formulations and proof hypotheses inspected; complex orientation, fixed tangent invariants, character weights, AC and Thom scope match the uses.
