The compact page qftx-borel-localization and its central theorem were inspected as context. Its statement concerns compact smooth manifolds and ordinary Borel cohomology. This batch proves the noncompact Borel–Moore result from finite invariant affine charts and six-functor localization; it does not infer the target theorem from the compact theorem.

## Source reading

- Edidin–Graham, https://arxiv.org/pdf/alg-geom/9508001, full 19-page paper: read Sections 2–4, including the equivariant Chow model, Proposition 3/Theorem 1 nonfixed-locus annihilation/localization proof, Proposition 4 normal Euler invertibility, and Theorem 2 fixed-component formula. It supports the independent localization cross-check and the Euler-denominator route. Its proof uses its own Sumihiro/stabilizer-stratum route and its groups are equivariant Chow groups; neither is silently substituted for this batch’s explicit finite-affine Borel–Moore argument.
- Ginzburg, https://arxiv.org/pdf/math/9802004, full 57-page Montreal lecture notes: read Section 1’s Borel–Moore definitions, proper pushforward, closed/open long exact sequence, duality and fundamental classes, and Section 12’s homotopy quotient, coefficient action, algebraic-group/maximal-compact comparison, and equivariant characteristic classes. These notes support the Borel and BM foundations; they do not prove the target noncompact localization theorem.
- Browser retrieval exposed the complete PDFs and relevant arguments. source-fetch-check --stamp remains pending for the batch coverage artifact; no retrieval failure or recovery attempt has occurred.

## Authored items

- def-qftx-localized-equivariant-borel-moore-data: defines T=(C*)^r, maximal compact K, product right Milnor conventions, R_T=Q[u_i], character multiplicative set, normalized BM grading, proper/open operations, cap action and smooth fundamental classes. Direct dependencies: the imported equivariant-BM definition, six-functor theorem, batch-8 rational torus classifying-space lemma, and AC. Level 1. Local verification states the stable 2rm approximation shift, coefficient convention and K subset T Borel comparison.
- lem-qftx-eigenfunction-open-bm-annihilation: for f(t x)=chi(t)f(x), the nowhere-zero eigenfunction gives a section of the associated character line on D(f); its Chern class kills equivariant BM there and on every invariant open restriction. The sign convention is fixed; the inverse character would differ by a sign but gives the same localization. Direct dependencies: the preceding definition, zero-section Euler definition, and complex diagonal-Thom/six-functor lemma. Level 2.
- thm-qftx-finite-affine-atlas-bm-concentration: on each invariant affine chart, finite weight generators cover the nonfixed locus by principal eigenfunction opens; finite Čech/Mayer–Vietoris and closed/open BM localization give concentration. Direct dependencies: eigenfunction annihilation, normalized BM data, six-functor localization, and exactness of module localization. Level 3. The proof is local to the finite affine cover and does not import Sumihiro or compactness of X.
- lem-qftx-fixed-embedding-bm-euler-self-intersection: the fixed scheme is smooth with invariant tangent space and nontrivial normal weights; normalized Thom/Gysin gives self-intersection, and a weight-product leading term plus compact positive-degree nilpotence gives a localized Euler inverse for proper F. Added direct dependencies on the batch-8 proper Borel-base lemma and rational torus cohomology, plus pinned Künneth and Whitney-Thom suppliers; the original plan list did not make these exact uses direct. The page already requires the corresponding Borel and Thom categories. Level 2; the batch-8 direct suppliers inspected for this proof are hash-current ready.
- def-qftx-proper-fixed-locus-localized-pushforward: defines the map as the proper trace of the inverse concentration isomorphism, with Borel–Moore grading and complex fundamental-class insertion explicit. Direct dependencies: concentration and normalized BM data. Level 4.
- thm-qftx-proper-fixed-locus-noncompact-localization: proves cover independence, functoriality for proper equivariant maps, agreement with genuine pushforward when X is proper, the fixed-component Euler denominator formula, and empty/finite/rank-zero cases. Direct dependencies: proper-locus pushforward definition, fixed-embedding self-intersection/Euler lemma, and concentration. Level 5. A TikZ commutative square is included only as exposition; the proof does not rely on it.
- ex-qftx-localized-bm-affine-plane: diagonal T=(C*)^2 action on C^2, one affine invariant chart, proper origin, tangent character Euler product u_1u_2, and localized fundamental pushforward 1/(u_1u_2). Direct dependencies: the localization theorem, localized BM data, and fixed-normal Euler lemma. Level 6.
- ex-qftx-localized-bm-proper-fixed-component: T scales the C factor of P^1 times C; the two standard charts form a finite invariant affine cover, F=P^1 is proper, the normal Euler class is u, and the point-Gysin class h has trace one, giving 1/u. Direct dependencies add the Thom theorem for the explicit point class. Level 6.
- ex-qftx-nonproper-fixed-locus-excluded: trivial action on C* gives F=C*; a closed subset after base change to A^1 has nonclosed image, so the proper-trace definition supplies no value. Direct dependencies: localized BM data and the proper-fixed-locus pushforward definition. Level 5.
- All nine assigned item carriers and both frontmatter-only page files are now present. The fixed-normal Euler proof promotes Künneth, Whitney–Thom multiplicativity, rational torus cohomology and the proper Borel-base result to explicit direct dependencies; all uses are in the current math page requirements or its imported mathematical closure. The proper-component example directly depends on the Thom theorem for its point Gysin class.

